We are pleased to submit our proposal in response to the call for tenders issued by the City of Belval for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist agents in their administrative activities. Our team has carefully reviewed the requirements and constraints outlined in the tender document, and we are confident that our proposed solution meets the needs of the City of Belval.

**Introduction**

The City of Belval is seeking to improve the efficiency and quality of its administrative services by implementing an artificial intelligence (AI) solution that can assist agents in their daily tasks. The solution should provide quick access to reliable and up-to-date information, facilitate the consultation of internal procedures and applicable regulations, and enable the sharing of relevant information between agents and services. Our proposal outlines a comprehensive approach to designing and deploying an AI-powered intelligent assistance tool that meets these requirements.

**Solution Overview**

Our proposed solution is based on a sovereign AI model that can be fine-tuned on a domain-specific corpus to provide contextualized answers to agents' queries. The model will be integrated with existing business software, such as civil status and town planning systems, electronic document management (EDM), and user directories. The solution will also include a user-friendly interface that allows agents to easily interact with the system and access relevant information.

**Key Features**

Our proposed solution includes the following key features:

1. **Assistance with information consultation**: Our AI-powered tool will provide agents with quick access to reliable and up-to-date information from internal procedures, applicable regulations, and other relevant sources.
2. **Drafting of administrative contents**: The tool will assist agents in drafting administrative letters, answers to users, and syntheses of files, ensuring that the content is accurate and compliant with regulatory requirements.
3. **Contextualization of answers**: Our solution will take into account the context of the agent's query and provide relevant and personalized responses.
4. **Sharing of relevant information**: The tool will enable agents to share relevant information with each other and with other services, facilitating collaboration and ensuring continuity of processing.
5. **Compliance with regulatory requirements**: Our solution will ensure that all responses and recommendations provided by the AI-powered tool comply with applicable regulations and internal procedures.

**Technical Specifications**

Our proposed solution will be based on a cloud-based infrastructure that ensures high availability and scalability. The solution will be hosted on a SecNumCloud-type infrastructure, which guarantees the sovereignty of data and compliance with regulatory requirements. Our team will work closely with the City of Belval's IT department to ensure seamless integration with existing systems and infrastructure.

**Deployment and Training**

We propose a progressive deployment approach, starting with a pilot phase that covers a limited scope and gradually expanding to all services. Our team will provide comprehensive training to agents on the use of the AI-powered tool, ensuring that they are comfortable and confident in using the system.

**Evaluation Criteria**

Our proposal will be evaluated based on the following criteria:

1. **Quality and relevance of the proposed solution**: Our team will demonstrate the effectiveness of our AI-powered tool in providing accurate and relevant responses to agents' queries.
2. **Compliance with regulatory requirements**: We will ensure that our solution complies with all applicable regulations and internal procedures.
3. **Level of security**: Our solution will guarantee the sovereignty of data and comply with SecNumCloud standards.
4. **Global cost of the proposed solution**: We will provide a detailed breakdown of the costs associated with our proposal, including deployment, maintenance, and training.
5. **Capacity for innovation**: Our team will demonstrate the potential for innovation and improvement in our proposed solution.

**Conclusion**

In conclusion, our proposal outlines a comprehensive approach to designing and deploying an AI-powered intelligent assistance tool that meets the needs of the City of Belval. We are confident that our solution will improve the efficiency and quality of administrative services, provide quick access to reliable and up-to-date information, and facilitate collaboration between agents and services. We look forward to the opportunity to discuss our proposal in further detail and demonstrate the effectiveness of our AI-powered tool.
